---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/documents.css';
const issueUrl='https://github.com/badjoke-lab/crypto-yield-archive/issues/new?template=correction.yml';
const repoUrl='https://github.com/badjoke-lab/crypto-yield-archive';
---
<BaseLayout title="Corrections | Crypto Yield Archive" description="How to report corrections and source improvements for Crypto Yield Archive records.">
<header class="document-head"><div><p class="kicker">Record maintenance</p><h1>Submit a correction</h1><p class="lede">Corrections are most useful when they identify the affected page, the disputed or missing claim, and the evidence supporting a change.</p><div class="document-actions"><a class="ghost-button" href={issueUrl}>Open correction issue</a><a class="text-action" href={repoUrl}>View repository →</a></div></div><dl class="document-facts"><div><dt>Route</dt><dd>GitHub issue</dd></div><div><dt>Preferred evidence</dt><dd>Primary sources</dd></div><div><dt>Review model</dt><dd>Manual</dd></div><div><dt>Unknowns</dt><dd>Allowed</dd></div></dl></header>
<section class="document-section" style="margin-top:42px"><p class="kicker">Correction checklist</p><h2>What to include</h2><div class="correction-steps"><article><span>01</span><h3>Page URL</h3><p>The CYA page where the issue appears.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Platform name</h3><p>The platform record affected by the correction.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Claim</h3><p>The date, status, outcome, event, terms-risk interpretation, or source that appears wrong or incomplete.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Sources</h3><p>Official statements, court documents, regulatory notices, archived pages, or reputable reporting.</p></article></div></section>
<div class="document-layout"><nav class="document-nav"><a href="#sources">Preferred sources</a><a href="#changes">What may change</a><a href="#uncertainty">Uncertainty</a><a href="#related">Related pages</a></nav><article class="document-prose"><section id="sources" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">01</p><h2>Preferred sources</h2><p>Official statements, court and bankruptcy documents, regulatory notices, archived website captures, and high-quality reporting are preferred over unsourced summaries or isolated social posts.</p></section><section id="changes" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">02</p><h2>What CYA may change</h2><p>A correction can update entity facts, chronology, customer outcome, terms risk, URL or archive status, evidence links, reliability labels, or uncertainty notes.</p></section><section id="uncertainty" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">03</p><h2>Uncertainty is allowed</h2><p>If available sources do not support a final conclusion, the record should remain unknown, unresolved, or medium confidence rather than being forced into a stronger claim.</p></section><section id="related" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">04</p><h2>Related pages</h2><div class="document-actions"><a class="text-action" href="/source-quality/">Source quality →</a><a class="text-action" href="/methodology/">Methodology →</a><a class="text-action" href="/timeline/">Timeline →</a></div></section></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
